(PRC-29 — `Pivot root to "<new_root>" with old root "<put_old>".` performs
 pivot_root(2).
 Also covers: PRC-32 (the error flag is set on failure).
 SAFETY / LIMIT: pivot_root(2) needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so this returns EPERM
 and the root filesystem is untouched. The success-path claims — PRC-30
 (put_old must already exist inside new_root) and PRC-31 (the old root
 then lives at put_old and should be released with `Unmount ... lazily`) —
 are NOT verified by this probe and cannot be without root or a user
 namespace.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-29.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   pivot root set the error flag
   the root filesystem is unchanged and execution continued
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot/oldroot".
Pivot root to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot" with old root "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot/oldroot".
On error print "pivot root set the error flag".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot/oldroot".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_newroot".
print "the root filesystem is unchanged and execution continued".
